Package: trialplate
Type: Package
Title: Sample-Size Diagnostics for Data-Driven Trial Eligibility Criteria
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Runshu", "Wang", email = "runshu.wang@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Tools for evaluating rules that relax clinical-trial eligibility
    criteria from data. Shapley main effects and pairwise interaction indices for
    eligibility criteria are computed by exact enumeration on two benefit
    estimands in parallel, the log hazard ratio and the difference in restricted
    mean survival time, because the hazard ratio is non-collapsible and the two
    can disagree. The package supplies the diagnostics that such analyses need
    before they are trusted: a closed-form interaction leverage that says whether
    a criterion pair can exhibit an interaction at all, a logical-implication
    detector for criteria that make their interaction cell an arithmetic
    identity, and out-of-sample evaluation of a selection rule against the
    protocol it replaces. Estimation kernels are written for the one-binary-
    covariate weighted Cox and weighted Kaplan-Meier problems that dominate the
    2^p enumeration, and agree with 'survival' to near machine precision.
